config VIDEO_MTK_IMGSYS
	tristate "MediaTek MT6735 IMGSYS/ISP platform driver"
	depends on MEDIA_SUPPORT
	depends on VIDEO_DEV
	depends on COMMON_CLK
	depends on OF
	depends on PM
	help
	  Platform, clock, power and reset driver for the MediaTek MT6735 /
	  MT6737T image signal processor (IMGSYS) block.

	  The driver owns the ISP core register windows, the six IMGSYS clock
	  gates and the ISP power domain, performs the documented Pass 1,
	  Pass 2, CAMSV and CAMSV2 soft resets on probe, and exposes the
	  mapped register windows through debugfs for diagnostics.

	  The ISP capture pipeline itself is not implemented: running the
	  Pass 1 / Pass 2 / CAM_SV / DSP pipelines and the on-demand
	  ISP_RESET_* ioctls requires the proprietary MTK camera userspace ABI
	  (libcamdrv) plus the ISP firmware images, neither of which is
	  available.  That part, including the deterministic reset sequences,
	  is implemented by the separate "camera-isp" character driver
	  (CONFIG_VIDEO_MTK_ISP), which maps the same windows itself.  This
	  driver therefore provides no V4L2 entity and no video node.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will
	  be called mtk-imgsys.
